        /// <summary>
        /// Resolve the label in force for named events, as of each event&#39;s own horizon Answers, for each named event, which assertion was in force AS OF that event&#39;s own horizon — and what disagreed with it.  This is the join surface: the dataset materialiser calls it to attach ground truth to training rows, and the evaluator calls it to score a past decision against what was knowable when the decision had to be made. One mechanism for both, so a model can never be trained under one leakage rule and scored under another.  Three answers are distinct and all three are honest: a resolved label, an event that has not matured, and a matured event nobody has judged. The last is never reported as unproductive.
